@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
title Resonance - logical modules and implementation status
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
actor Listener
cloud Discord
package "One local Python application" {
  component "Discord adapter\nbot.main / ResonanceBot / ping" as adapter <<implemented>>
  component "Player and library\nqueue, controls, file discovery" as player <<planned>>
  component "User and music data\nprofiles, ratings, history" as users <<planned>>
  component "Recommendations and analytics\nbaseline, TF-IDF, evaluation, CSV" as recs <<planned>>
}
database "SQLite\nschema draft: PR #26" as db
folder "Local music" as music
artifact "CSV experiments\npseudonym_id" as csv
Listener --> Discord
Discord <--> adapter
adapter ..> player
adapter ..> users
adapter ..> recs
player ..> music
player ..> users : playback activity
users ..> db
recs ..> db : ratings and catalogue
recs ..> csv
note bottom of db
Schema exists on database/initial-schema.
Runtime database access is not integrated.
SQLCipher driver / key handling remain undecided.
end note
note bottom of recs
Optional vector index is outside the current scope.
Logical modules share one process, not microservices.
end note
legend right
Solid arrows: current interactions
Dotted arrows: planned integrations
endlegend
@enduml
